# Lean / Lake build artifacts
lean/.lake/
# lean/lake-manifest.json is deliberately TRACKED: it pins the exact Mathlib
# and toolchain revisions the build was verified against, so `lake build` is
# reproducible rather than resolving fresh each time.
**/.olean
**/.ilean

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated data -- everything except the provenance manifest
data/*
!data/manifest.json

# The quotable figures file IS tracked: the phase documents cite it by key, and
# a gitignored copy could not keep prose and data in step (risk R-002).
!data/phase2_figures.json

# data/phase1_figures.json is tracked for the same reason as the artifact
# above: the Phase 1 documents quote it by key, and tests/test_figure_tags.py
# fails when a quoted literal and the generated value disagree. A gitignored
# figures file could not keep prose and data in step on a clean clone.
!data/phase1_figures.json

# The artifacts cited as evidence by `verified-numeric` claims are tracked too,
# and for the same reason: `scripts/check_claims.py` now requires every cited
# artifact to exist and to match its `data/manifest.json` SHA-256, so a claim
# whose evidence is absent on a clean clone must fail rather than pass silently.
# Ten claims cited these four and none of them survived a fresh checkout.
# 24 KB in total. Artifacts that no claim cites stay ignored.
!data/phase1_summary.json
!data/phase0_5_gate.csv
!data/phase2_bounds.csv
!data/phase2_residual.csv

# The Phase 1 exact-value ladder IS tracked (37 rows, 4 KB): it is the oracle
# the Phase 2 bound tests compare T1, T3 and T5 against. While it was ignored,
# a clean clone had no oracle and those twelve comparisons SKIPPED rather than
# ran -- the gate silently did not exist for anyone but the machine that
# generated the file. Its provenance (script, git rev, SHA-256) is recorded in
# data/manifest.json and asserted by tests/test_phase2_bounds.py, so the
# tracked copy cannot drift from what scripts/run_phase1.py produced.
!data/phase1_data.csv

# Generated figures
figures/*.png
figures/*.pdf
